<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's Somague expects to pay dividend.</title>
<headline>Portugal's Somague expects to pay dividend.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese construction company Somague-SGPS expects to pay a dividend of around 20 escudos per share on its 1996 results after two years in which no payout was made, company vice-president Diogo Vaz Guedes told Reuters.</p>
<p>The last time that Somague gave a dividend was in 1993 when it paid a net 16 escudos per share.</p>
<p>Somague forecasts a net consolidated profit of one billion escudos in 1996 from sales of between 48 and 49 billion. In 1995, it made 331 million escudos on sales of 36.3 billion.</p>
<p>($1=165.61 escudos)</p>
<p>--Jose Barata, Lisbon bureau 3511-3113121</p>
